{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .pose/specs/pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md | sed -n '1,210p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go | sed -n '235,285p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim.go | sed -n '1,100p'\"","aggregated_output":"nl: .pose/specs/pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md: No such file or directory\n   235\t\t\tnames = append(names, \"HOME\", \"USERPROFILE\")\n   236\t\t} else {\n   237\t\t\tnames = append(names, a.Containment.Environment...)\n   238\t\t}\n   239\t\tvalues := map[string]string{}\n   240\t\tput := func(name, value string) {\n   241\t\t\tif runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" {\n   242\t\t\t\tname = strings.ToUpper(name)\n   243\t\t\t}\n   244\t\t\tvalues[name] = value\n   245\t\t}\n   246\t\tfor _, name := range names {\n   247\t\t\tif value, ok := os.LookupEnv(name); ok {\n   248\t\t\t\tput(name, value)\n   249\t\t\t}\n   250\t\t}\n   251\t\tsecrets := []string{}\n   252\t\tif a.Containment != nil {\n   253\t\t\tfor _, name := range a.Containment.Credentials {\n   254\t\t\t\tif value, ok := os.LookupEnv(name); ok && value != \"\" {\n   255\t\t\t\t\tif len(value) < 8 || len(value) > 64<<10 {\n   256\t\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"authorized credential value has unsupported length\")\n   257\t\t\t\t\t}\n   258\t\t\t\t\tif strings.Contains(brief, value) || strings.Contains(notes, value) {\n   259\t\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"brief/notes contain an authorized credential; refusing execution\")\n   260\t\t\t\t\t}\n   261\t\t\t\t\tput(name, value)\n   262\t\t\t\t\tsecrets = append(secrets, value)\n   263\t\t\t\t}\n   264\t\t\t}\n   265\t\t\tvalues[\"HOME\"] = tmp\n   266\t\t\tvalues[\"USERPROFILE\"] = tmp\n   267\t\t}\n   268\t\tvalues[\"TMPDIR\"] = tmp\n   269\t\tvalues[\"TMP\"] = tmp\n   270\t\tvalues[\"TEMP\"] = tmp\n   271\t\tkeys := make([]string, 0, len(values))\n   272\t\tfor k := range values {\n   273\t\t\tkeys = append(keys, k)\n   274\t\t}\n   275\t\tsort.Strings(keys)\n   276\t\tenv := make([]string, 0, len(keys))\n   277\t\tfor _, k := range keys {\n   278\t\t\tenv = append(env, k+\"=\"+values[k])\n   279\t\t}\n   280\t\t// Replace overlapping credentials longest first so no residual suffix leaks.\n   281\t\tsort.Slice(secrets, func(i, j int) bool { return len(secrets[i]) > len(secrets[j]) })\n   282\t\treturn env, secrets, nil\n   283\t}\n   284\t\n   285\t// A single longest-first replacement pass handles overlapping session and\n     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\t// The review run shim (spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes,\n     4\t// review rounds 6 and 8): a descendant of the reviewer that leaves the\n     5\t// adapter's process group, starts its own session and clears its environment\n     6\t// matches neither the group kill nor the sealed-checkout entry. Making the\n     7\t// dispatcher a child subreaper caught it, but a subreaper is process-wide:\n     8\t// in the dispatching process it also adopted and ended children other code\n     9\t// started there (a detached delegation), and reaped processes another\n    10\t// goroutine was waiting for. The dispatcher therefore starts the adapter\n    11\t// through a shim, the same executable re-entered with ReviewShimArg, which\n    12\t// makes itself the subreaper, runs the adapter, and, once it exits, ends\n    13\t// every process left in its subtree. The shim has no other children, so\n    14\t// everything it adopts is the run's.\n    15\t\n    16\t// ReviewShimArg is the first argument that runs the executable as a review\n    17\t// run shim instead of the CLI.\n    18\tconst ReviewShimArg = \"__pose-review-run-shim\"\n    19\t\n    20\t// ReviewShimReportEnv names the file the shim writes its report to.\n    21\tconst ReviewShimReportEnv = \"POSE_REVIEW_SHIM_REPORT\"\n    22\t\n    23\t// ReviewShimAvailable says the running executable handles ReviewShimArg. It\n    24\t// is set by the pose command and by the test binaries that dispatch; any\n    25\t// other embedder starts the adapter directly, without the shim.\n    26\tvar ReviewShimAvailable = false\n    27\t\n    28\t// reviewShimReport is what the shim found after the adapter exited.\n    29\ttype reviewShimReport struct {\n    30\t\tEnded []string `json:\"ended\"`\n    31\t\tError string   `json:\"error,omitempty\"`\n    32\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
