SE checks the conclusion before it records it, and refuses the whole draft when one rule breaks: (a) a `passed` criterion of kind judgment carries a `rationale` saying what you examined and what you concluded; (b) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is exactly one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence (`<class>:<id>`, of a class the criterion asks for when it names one), never a file and line, a command or a structural fact id: those go in a finding or in the `rationale`; (c) a criterion disposed `finding` carries as its `evidence` the `id` of a finding listed in `findings`, and that finding is open until you give it `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; (d) each structural fact listed above is answered by the criterion that asks for structural mapping, as its `mappings`: `[{\\\"delta\\\": <fact id>, \\\"basis\\\": <requirement or decision ref>, \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": <why>}]`, or `not-applicable` with the reason; (e) a `not-applicable` carries a `rationale` and is refused when the bundle seals evidence of a class the criterion asks for; (f) every required criterion and every tool above is answered; (g) the `disposition` of a tool is `passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else (`not-run` is refused); a tool listed as required must be run and `passed`, with the ref of the sealed evidence it produced as `evidence` when it names classes, and `not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists; a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; (h) the `evidence` of a tool is `<class>:<ref>`: when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed (listed under Sealed evidence), otherwise `command:` followed by the command you ran; a bare command line is refused; (i) a draft that approves leaves no finding open: each finding is either a follow-up with `action`, `owner` and `review_by`, which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes; a finding without them is open and the approval is refused.\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:121:// precondition is the completion of the review is answered deferred, the component scoping of\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:132:\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`;\", \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; a required tool whose precondition is the completion of the review (`review-check`, `closeout-check`) cannot pass before your attestation: answer it `deferred` with a `rationale`;\", 1)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:137:\treturn text + \" (j) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is of a class the criterion asks for and, when the criterion or tool belongs to a component, of that component (the Sealed evidence list names the module of each ref); (k) the `basis` of a mapping is a requirement or decision id of the scope's spec, such as R1 or D1.\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:511:\t\t\tline(\"%d. In the same block, the conclusion POSE records as the attestation: `criteria` (one entry per criterion above, each with `id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>` — a class the criterion asks for when it names one — and `rationale` for not-applicable), and `tools` (one entry per tool above, each with `id`, `component` when it has one, `disposition`, `evidence` and `rationale`). A follow-up finding that should be accepted as a risk carries `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; any other finding stays open. A criterion or tool you do not answer is not answered for you.\", next+1)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions_test.go:38:\t\tdraft.Tools = append(draft.Tools, ReviewDraftTool{ID: tool.ID, Component: tool.Component, Disposition: tool.Disposition, Evidence: tool.Evidence, Rationale: tool.Rationale})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:151:\t\ttools = append(tools, ReviewToolDisposition{ID: t.ID, Component: t.Component, Disposition: t.Disposition, Evidence: t.Evidence, Rationale: t.Rationale})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:178:// deferred, a recommended tool not used. A required tool left out stays out,\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:192:\t\t\tout = append(out, ReviewToolDisposition{ID: tool.ID, Component: tool.Component, Disposition: \"deferred\", Rationale: \"post-review gate\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:194:\t\t\tout = append(out, ReviewToolDisposition{ID: tool.ID, Component: tool.Component, Disposition: \"not-used\", Rationale: \"not used during review\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:257:// a post-review gate deferred and a recommended tool not used state none,\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:268:\t\tif ok && t.Evidence == \"\" && (t.Disposition == \"deferred\" && containsString(tool.Preconditions, \"review-complete\") || t.Disposition == \"not-used\" && tool.Requiredness == \"recommended\") {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go | sed -n '178,285p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go | sed -n '112,140p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go | sed -n '178,285p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go | sed -n '112,140p'\"","aggregated_output":"   178\t// deferred, a recommended tool not used. A required tool left out stays out,\n   179\t// for the domain writer to name. `review attest` and a run's conclusion fill\n   180\t// the same defaults, so a run's conclusion and its attestation agree on them.\n   181\tfunc ReviewToolDefaults(plan []ReviewPlanTool, given []ReviewToolDisposition) []ReviewToolDisposition {\n   182\t\tout := append([]ReviewToolDisposition{}, given...)\n   183\t\tprovided := map[string]bool{}\n   184\t\tfor _, t := range given {\n   185\t\t\tprovided[t.ID+\"\\x00\"+t.Component] = true\n   186\t\t}\n   187\t\tfor _, tool := range plan {\n   188\t\t\tif provided[tool.ID+\"\\x00\"+tool.Component] {\n   189\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   190\t\t\t}\n   191\t\t\tif containsString(tool.Preconditions, \"review-complete\") {\n   192\t\t\t\tout = append(out, ReviewToolDisposition{ID: tool.ID, Component: tool.Component, Disposition: \"deferred\", Rationale: \"post-review gate\"})\n   193\t\t\t} else if tool.Requiredness == \"recommended\" {\n   194\t\t\t\tout = append(out, ReviewToolDisposition{ID: tool.ID, Component: tool.Component, Disposition: \"not-used\", Rationale: \"not used during review\"})\n   195\t\t\t}\n   196\t\t}\n   197\t\treturn out\n   198\t}\n   199\t\n   200\tfunc findingEvidence(f ReviewDraftFinding) string {\n   201\t\tif f.File == \"\" {\n   202\t\t\treturn \"\"\n   203\t\t}\n   204\t\tif f.Line > 0 {\n   205\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"file:%s:%d\", f.File, f.Line)\n   206\t\t}\n   207\t\treturn \"file:\" + f.File\n   208\t}\n   209\t\n   210\t// runConclusionDiffers is why att does not state the typed conclusion of a\n   211\t// run briefed to write one (template review-brief/3), or \"\": its criteria,\n   212\t// tools and findings are the ones the run's draft concludes, whoever signs\n   213\t// it. A run briefed with an earlier template carried no typed conclusion and\n   214\t// binds only its decision, as before (review round 1, B1; decision D1).\n   215\tfunc runConclusionDiffers(run ReviewRun, bundle ReviewBundle, att ReviewAttestation) string {\n   216\t\tif run.Provenance == nil || !reviewBriefAsksConclusion(run.Provenance.TemplateVersion) {\n   217\t\t\treturn \"\"\n   218\t\t}\n   219\t\tdraft, err := ParseReviewDraft(run.Output)\n   220\t\tif err != nil {\n   221\t\t\treturn \"the run's draft cannot be read: \" + err.Error()\n   222\t\t}\n   223\t\tif draft == nil {\n   224\t\t\tdraft = &ReviewDraft{Decision: att.Decision}\n   225\t\t}\n   226\t\twant := reviewAttestationFromDraft(run, bundle, *draft, att.Reviewer)\n   227\t\tvar differ []string\n   228\t\tdiffer = append(differ, differingItems(\"criterion\", mappingsByDelta(att.Criteria), mappingsByDelta(want.Criteria))...)\n   229\t\tdiffer = append(differ, differingItems(\"tool\", concludingTools(bundle.Payload.Plan.Tools, att.Tools), concludingTools(bundle.Payload.Plan.Tools, want.Tools))...)\n   230\t\tdiffer = append(differ, differingItems(\"finding\", att.Findings, want.Findings)...)\n   231\t\tif len(differ) > 0 {\n   232\t\t\treturn strings.Join(differ, \"; \")\n   233\t\t}\n   234\t\treturn \"\"\n   235\t}\n   236\t\n   237\t// mappingsByDelta is criteria with each one's mappings ordered by delta: the\n   238\t// order a writer lists them in states nothing (review round 2, F1).\n   239\tfunc mappingsByDelta(criteria []ReviewCriterion) []ReviewCriterion {\n   240\t\tout := make([]ReviewCriterion, 0, len(criteria))\n   241\t\tfor _, c := range criteria {\n   242\t\t\tc.Mappings = append([]ReviewCriterionMapping(nil), c.Mappings...)\n   243\t\t\tsort.SliceStable(c.Mappings, func(i, j int) bool {\n   244\t\t\t\ta, _ := json.Marshal(c.Mappings[i])\n   245\t\t\t\tb, _ := json.Marshal(c.Mappings[j])\n   246\t\t\t\treturn c.Mappings[i].Delta < c.Mappings[j].Delta || c.Mappings[i].Delta == c.Mappings[j].Delta && string(a) < string(b)\n   247\t\t\t})\n   248\t\t\tif len(c.Mappings) == 0 {\n   249\t\t\t\tc.Mappings = nil\n   250\t\t\t}\n   251\t\t\tout = append(out, c)\n   252\t\t}\n   253\t\treturn out\n   254\t}\n   255\t\n   256\t// concludingTools are the dispositions of tools that state a conclusion:\n   257\t// a post-review gate deferred and a recommended tool not used state none,\n   258\t// whatever their rationale says, so a writer that fills them is not\n   259\t// answering for the reviewer.\n   260\tfunc concludingTools(plan []ReviewPlanTool, tools []ReviewToolDisposition) []ReviewToolDisposition {\n   261\t\tplanned := map[string]ReviewPlanTool{}\n   262\t\tfor _, tool := range plan {\n   263\t\t\tplanned[tool.ID+\"\\x00\"+tool.Component] = tool\n   264\t\t}\n   265\t\tout := []ReviewToolDisposition{}\n   266\t\tfor _, t := range tools {\n   267\t\t\ttool, ok := planned[t.ID+\"\\x00\"+t.Component]\n   268\t\t\tif ok && t.Evidence == \"\" && (t.Disposition == \"deferred\" && containsString(tool.Preconditions, \"review-complete\") || t.Disposition == \"not-used\" && tool.Requiredness == \"recommended\") {\n   269\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   270\t\t\t}\n   271\t\t\tout = append(out, t)\n   272\t\t}\n   273\t\treturn out\n   274\t}\n   275\t\n   276\t// differingItems names the items of got and want, keyed by id and\n   277\t// component, that one has and the other lacks or states differently.\n   278\tfunc differingItems[T any](kind string, got, want []T) []string {\n   279\t\tindex := func(items []T) (map[string]string, []string) {\n   280\t\t\tout, keys := map[string]string{}, []string{}\n   281\t\t\tfor _, v := range items {\n   282\t\t\t\traw, _ := json.Marshal(v)\n   283\t\t\t\tvar m struct {\n   284\t\t\t\t\tID        string `json:\"id\"`\n   285\t\t\t\t\tComponent string `json:\"component\"`\n   112\t\treturn reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template) || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateConclusions || template == reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion\n   113\t}\n   114\t\n   115\t// briefRulesTextV5 is the statement of the rules the conclusion is checked against that\n   116\t// review-brief/4 and /5 carry, byte for byte; a version never changes its text.\n   117\tconst briefRulesTextV5 = \"POSE checks the conclusion before it records it, and refuses the whole draft when one rule breaks: (a) a `passed` criterion of kind judgment carries a `rationale` saying what you examined and what you concluded; (b) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is exactly one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence (`<class>:<id>`, of a class the criterion asks for when it names one), never a file and line, a command or a structural fact id: those go in a finding or in the `rationale`; (c) a criterion disposed `finding` carries as its `evidence` the `id` of a finding listed in `findings`, and that finding is open until you give it `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; (d) each structural fact listed above is answered by the criterion that asks for structural mapping, as its `mappings`: `[{\\\"delta\\\": <fact id>, \\\"basis\\\": <requirement or decision ref>, \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": <why>}]`, or `not-applicable` with the reason; (e) a `not-applicable` carries a `rationale` and is refused when the bundle seals evidence of a class the criterion asks for; (f) every required criterion and every tool above is answered; (g) the `disposition` of a tool is `passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else (`not-run` is refused); a tool listed as required must be run and `passed`, with the ref of the sealed evidence it produced as `evidence` when it names classes, and `not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists; a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; (h) the `evidence` of a tool is `<class>:<ref>`: when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed (listed under Sealed evidence), otherwise `command:` followed by the command you ran; a bare command line is refused; (i) a draft that approves leaves no finding open: each finding is either a follow-up with `action`, `owner` and `review_by`, which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes; a finding without them is open and the approval is refused.\"\n   118\t\n   119\t// briefRulesText is the statement of those rules in the brief of template. review-brief/6 also\n   120\t// says which severities the sealed policy lets a follow-up be accepted at, that a tool whose\n   121\t// precondition is the completion of the review is answered deferred, the component scoping of\n   122\t// evidence, and what a mapping's basis is.\n   123\tfunc briefRulesText(template string, bundle ReviewBundle) string {\n   124\t\tif template != reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules && !reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template) {\n   125\t\t\treturn briefRulesTextV5\n   126\t\t}\n   127\t\ttext := briefRulesTextV5\n   128\t\tseverities := strings.Join(bundle.Payload.SealedGates().AcceptedRiskSeverities, \", \")\n   129\t\tif severities == \"\" {\n   130\t\t\tseverities = \"none\"\n   131\t\t}\n   132\t\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`;\", \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; a required tool whose precondition is the completion of the review (`review-check`, `closeout-check`) cannot pass before your attestation: answer it `deferred` with a `rationale`;\", 1)\n   133\t\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes;\", \"which is recorded as an accepted risk only when its severity is one the sealed review policy accepts (\"+severities+\"), or the draft requests changes and any finding of another severity is fixed first;\", 1)\n   134\t\tif reviewBriefFromAllNotApplicable(template) {\n   135\t\t\ttext += \" (l) a draft that dispenses with every required criterion as `not-applicable` is refused: a scope whose whole plan is inapplicable is not reviewed by it;\"\n   136\t\t}\n   137\t\treturn text + \" (j) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is of a class the criterion asks for and, when the criterion or tool belongs to a component, of that component (the Sealed evidence list names the module of each ref); (k) the `basis` of a mapping is a requirement or decision id of the scope's spec, such as R1 or D1.\"\n   138\t}\n   139\t\n   140\t// reviewBriefStatesRules reports a template that states the rules the conclusion is\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
